rearrange components that way?

05:53.640 --> 05:54.640
Yeah, you could.

05:54.640 --> 05:55.640
Yeah, yeah.

05:55.640 --> 05:59.320
So because with the scope slot, I mean, you have free reign of like whatever you want

05:59.320 --> 06:00.880
that data to be used.

06:00.880 --> 06:04.320
And I mentioned this, I guess I didn't demo this early, but you can technically feed

06:04.320 --> 06:06.760
methods into it too, so functions.

06:06.760 --> 06:10.920
And so if you're like rearranging a modal, for example, and you know that it has a closed

06:10.920 --> 06:15.840
functionality already in your child, it doesn't necessarily make sense to like create something

06:15.840 --> 06:17.520
that like throws it to the parent.

06:17.520 --> 06:21.520
So through a scope slot, you could theoretically expose that method to that one section, call

06:21.520 --> 06:23.720
it like an action slot.

06:23.720 --> 06:26.960
And then in the action slot, you just create whatever button or arrow you want, and then

06:26.960 --> 06:30.520
just call like the child's closed method.

